      <abstract>
        <para>This article outlines the lifecycle policies and support timelines for software components in &suselinux; 15 that do not align with standard Service Pack releases. While &suselinux; 15 provides a 13-year general lifecycle, selected runtime environments, languages, and tools—such as Java, Python, Node.js, Go, and Rust—follow independent maintenance schedules or receive regular updates within released Service Packs. Use this guide to track support end dates, maintain security compliance, and plan application lifecycles across &suselinux; 15 Service Packs.</para>
